	init_flow_fine.f90: Enclose 'if(metal)' statements within 'if(star.or.sink)' statement, consistent with other subroutines, to avoid segmentation fault when eps_star = 0.

	SEE "IMPORTANT 1)" below

	28 FEB 2024:
	Added family tag, previously set to 0 by default, now set to the value specified by the ICs (if available)

About:

This subdirectory contains a number of patches to files originally in /Users/tepper/codes/ramses_fork/patch/init/dice/.

The modifications are intended to make this patch work with /Users/tepper/codes/ramses_fork/patch/tepper/oagertz/.

The necessary modifications have been accomplished by:
	1) Copying to this directory *all* the file in /Users/tepper/codes/ramses_fork/patch/init/dice/.
	2) Comparing with FileMerge the files *common* to the two above directories (add_list.f90, init_part.f90, particle_tree.f90), and adding the required code snippets
	3) Some files needed to be additionally edited by hand:
		- init_part.f90: make the zp array consistent with nmetals, i.e. 2D

Notes:
	- Some modifications are flagged by 'ERIC', 'EDGE2', or 'TTG', but not all
	- See also:
		/Users/tepper/codes/ramses_agertz/ramses/patch/dice/README
	- The bck_21DEC023 folder is temporary until I've made sure that the most recent update (22 DEC 2023) is working

IMPORTANT:

	1) These patches do not split all if-clauses of the form:

		if(star.or.sink)then
			if(metal)then
			endif
		endif
	into:
		if(star.or.sink)then
			...
		endif
		if(metal)then
			...
		endif

	as does my dice patch in, e.g. particle_tree.f90.
	MUST split these to allow metal advection for gas w | w/o cooling also when there is not star formation!

	2) From Tine Colman:
	"There are SOLVERmhd blocks [in the following files] but this file is not compatible with MHD:

		- init_flow_fine.f90

	It doesn't take into account that for MHD nvar is at least 8.""
